          "text": "S3: Proof strategy and lemma decomposition.\n\n**Stipulation**\n\nFor arbitrary predicates\n`GBP BD OC ALLOW : Transition \u2192 Prop`, assume:\n\n\\[\nhEval:\\forall t,\\ ALLOW(t)\\leftrightarrow GBP(t)\\land BD(t)\\land OC(t).\n\\]\n\nNo decidability, independence, or predicate semantics are assumed.\n\n**Generated claims**\n\nFor every transition `t`:\n\n1. **Necessity**\n   \\[\n   ALLOW(t)\\rightarrow GBP(t)\\land BD(t)\\land OC(t).\n   \\]\n\n2. **Sufficiency**\n   \\[\n   GBP(t)\\land BD(t)\\land OC(t)\\rightarrow ALLOW(t).\n   \\]\n\n3. **Necessary-and-sufficient characterization**\n   \\[\n   ALLOW(t)\\leftrightarrow GBP(t)\\land BD(t)\\land OC(t).\n   \\]\n\n**Proof strategy**\n\n- Derive necessity using the forward implication `(hEval t).mp`.\n- Derive sufficiency using the reverse implication `(hEval t).mpr`.\n- Construct the characterization from those two directional lemmas.\n- The proof is purely propositional; no case analysis or classical reasoning is required.\n\n**Lean 4 logical-core candidate**\n\n```lean\nuniverse u\n\nvariable {Transition : Type u}\nvariable {GBP BD OC ALLOW : Transition \u2192 Prop}\n\ntheorem allow_necessity\n    (hEval : \u2200 t, ALLOW t \u2194 GBP t \u2227 BD t \u2227 OC t)\n    (t : Transition)\n    (hAllow : ALLOW t) :\n    GBP t \u2227 BD t \u2227 OC t :=\n  (hEval t).mp hAllow\n\ntheorem allow_sufficiency\n    (hEval : \u2200 t, ALLOW t \u2194 GBP t \u2227 BD t \u2227 OC t)\n    (t : Transition)\n    (hConditions : GBP t \u2227 BD t \u2227 OC t) :\n    ALLOW t :=\n  (hEval t).mpr hConditions\n\ntheorem allow_admissible_iff\n    (hEval : \u2200 t, ALLOW t \u2194 GBP t \u2227 BD t \u2227 OC t)\n    (t : Transition) :\n    ALLOW t \u2194 GBP t \u2227 BD t \u2227 OC t := by\n  constructor\n  \u00b7 exact allow_necessity hEval t\n  \u00b7 exact allow_sufficiency hEval t\n```\n\n**Verified claims**\n\n- The theorem formulation and abstract evaluator equivalence are admitted from prior-stage artifacts.\n- No Lean compilation or proof-kernel verification is asserted at this stage.\n\n**Claim boundary and unresolved evidence**\n\nThese claims characterize only the stipulated abstract evaluator. No claim is made that any deployed or concrete GCAT/BCAT evaluator uses these predicates, satisfies `hEval`, or conforms to this Lean candidate. Implementation binding, compilation, and deployment conformance remain unresolved."
